Key objective — Provide transverse functional-safety and SOTIF authority across T1, T2 and T3.

Mission

Own the transverse functional-safety and SOTIF authority across the T1/T2/T3 stack, mirroring the cybersecurity authority. The mission covers ISO 26262, ISO 21448/SOTIF, HARA, safety concepts, safety requirements, ASIL arguments, ODD limitations, the evidence plan and the ability to challenge T1, T2 and T3 architectures whenever a safety assumption is not defensible. The role does not replace architects: it imposes the assurance framework and expected evidence.

Roles & responsibilities

- Define and maintain the ISO 26262 and ISO 21448/SOTIF assurance framework for T1/T2/T3.

- Lead HARA, safety goals, functional safety concept, technical safety concept and ASIL arguments where relevant.

- Define expected safety evidence for architecture, software, integration, HIL and field tests.

- Challenge ODD limitations, vehicle assumptions, degraded modes, command gate and autonomy functions.

- Maintain the safety case and unresolved safety assumptions visible to programme leadership.

- Align safety evidence with cyber, V&V and architecture decisions.

Skills

Hard skills

- ISO 26262;

- ISO 21448/SOTIF;

- HARA;

- safety goals;

- functional and technical safety concepts;

- ASIL argumentation;

- safety case;

- FMEA;

- FTA;

- assurance cases;

- requirements traceability.

Soft skills

- Independence;

- rigorous challenge;

- risk judgment;

- pedagogy;

- calm escalation;

- ability to arbitrate without unnecessary blocking.

Education & experience

10+ years in functional safety, SOTIF, safety assurance, automotive, rail, aerospace, defence or comparable safety-relevant engineering.

Success criteria after 12 months

Functional Safety & SOTIF framework baselined; HARA launched; safety goals and T1/T2/T3 assumptions traced; evidence plan established; safety interfaces with cyber, V&V and T1 ODD structured.

