Key objective — Provide the deterministic low-level execution platform for T1 safety-critical control.

Mission

Own low-level integration of the T1 software platform: safety-capable RTOS, BSP, board bring-up, partitioning, drivers, toolchains, protected endpoints and build reproducibility. The mission is to provide a deterministic and verifiable execution base for the T1 architecture without concentrating knowledge in a single person.

Roles & responsibilities

- Bring up and maintain the safety-capable RTOS, BSP and board-support baseline for T1.

- Integrate partitioning or freedom-from-interference mechanisms on the target compute architecture.

- Implement protected communication endpoints specified by the T1 architect and command-gate architect.

- Own low-level integration debugging, toolchains, reproducible builds and timing evidence.

- Define additional verification required by open or mixed software platforms.

- Support HW/SW defect analysis during bench, HIL and vehicle trials.

Skills

Hard skills

- Safety-capable RTOS;

- embedded C;

- BSP and board bring-up;

- lockstep MCU platforms;

- partitioning or hypervisors;

- E2E-protected communication;

- toolchains;

- low-level debugging.

Soft skills

- Hands-on pragmatism;

- systems debugging;

- patience;

- escalation clarity;

- reliability obsession;

- integration discipline.

Education & experience

6+ years in embedded/RTOS integration, BSP, board bring-up, safety-relevant platform engineering or comparable low-level systems integration.

Success criteria after 12 months

RTOS/BSP baseline started; partitioning approach selected; protected endpoints integration plan aligned with T1; timing and build evidence structure defined

