Key objective — Implement deterministic safety-critical control logic and the command gate that arbitrates actuator access.

Mission

Define and implement T1 safety-critical control behaviour. The mission covers drive-by-wire laws, command validation, the command gate, safe states, emergency stop, link-loss behaviour, degraded modes and the evidence that allows independent V&V to verify that T1 remains the final vehicle authority.

Roles & responsibilities

- Own drive-by-wire control logic, safe-state behaviours and command-validation implementation.

- Implement command-gate logic validating T2, T3 and certified-application requests before actuator access.

- Integrate deterministic envelope limits provided by the Vehicle Dynamics, Stability & T1 Operational Envelope Lead.

- Specify E-stop, link-loss, degraded-mode and transition behaviours with safety stakeholders.

- Define software requirements and evidence needed for independent V&V.

- Analyse field defects and update control behaviour without weakening the safety argument.

Skills

Hard skills

- Drive-by-wire;

- control engineering;

- embedded C;

- real-time software;

- state machines;

- safe-state design;

- MISRA-C;

- ASIL-D software discipline;

- timing and response-time analysis.

Soft skills

- Defensive engineering mindset;

- precision;

- calm under pressure;

- collaboration with safety;

- evidence culture;

- reliability focus.

Education & experience

8+ years in safety-critical embedded software, vehicle control, real-time control systems or comparable deterministic-command systems.

Success criteria after 12 months

Command-gate software baseline started; safe-state behaviours defined; T1 envelope limits integrated; timing budgets documented; first T1 software baseline ready for independent V&V.

